intro = [
    "Long ages past, in the world of Moratal, magic flowed through the land as an unending wellspring of power. It was wielded by mages, wizards, witches, and countless other power-born mortals. They stood beside kings as trusted advisers, turned the tide of great battles, and settled the disputes that divided kingdoms. Through their wisdom, nations prospered; through their might, empires rose and fell.",
    "Yet among these gifted souls, harmony did not endure. Several great factions of mages grew envious of one another, and their hearts became consumed by greed and ambition. No longer content with the power they possessed, they sought knowledge that had long been forbidden. Ancient tomes, forgotten scrolls, and relics hidden from mortal hands became the object of their relentless pursuit. In time, their search led them to a form of magic so unstable, and so immeasurably powerful, that its very existence threatened the world itself. It was known as Chronos Magic.",
    "Blinded by pride and driven by selfish desire, they unleashed Chronos Magic upon their rivals. Entire cities were laid to ruin. Villages were reduced to ash. Those they named enemies were, in truth, little more than innocent souls caught within their path. Harmless commoners were slaughtered. Mighty kings were struck down, their kingdoms broken and enslaved beneath the will of the mages. And among them all arose one whose mastery surpassed every other.",
    "He became the greatest wielder of Chronos Magic in all of Moratal. His thirst for knowledge knew no end. Wherever he journeyed, ruin followed. With every passing year he bent the laws of time further to his will, spreading chaos across the realm. Thus began the Time Wars, the darkest age Moratal had ever known.",
    "Such devastation could not remain unseen forever. At last, it drew the attention of an Ancient Being known only by a few... Time.",
    "The Mage understood what this meant. If he could seize the attention of Time itself, then perhaps he might uncover the path beyond creation—a passage into realms never meant for mortal feet. Yet his desire reached further still. He sought a place whispered of only in forgotten legends: A Golden Field, said to lie at the furthest reaches of existence. Knowing Time would one day come to end his destruction, the Mage devised a plan. He prepared for their meeting, believing he could bend even Time to his own purpose. And so, when Time came to confront him... He stood waiting.",
    "Time struck first, seeking to end the Mage's reign. Yet the Mage did not fall. His understanding of Chronos Magic had become so profound that he had learned to move beyond the ordinary flow of time itself. The powers of Time could no longer claim him. Not even Time could destroy him.",
    "Seeing this, the Mage laid forth his desire. He wished to pass beyond the mortal realm. Time refused. For Time alone knew the truth. There were indeed paths leading into the realms beyond—but to open them would demand a terrible price. The barrier between worlds could not be broken without bringing ruin upon Moratal itself.",
    "Thus Time offered the Mage a choice:'Release your hold upon this desire, and take my life alone...Or pursue the realms beyond, and doom this world to its end. Death shall await you in the realms ahead.'",
    "The Mage accepted the bargain and demanded to know what must be done. Yet before another word could be spoken... Time burst forth in a blinding light. Choosing sacrifice over destruction, Time surrendered His own existence that Moratal might endure. In so doing, He granted the Mage the very thing he had desired, while sparing the world from the devastation that would otherwise have consumed it.",
    "When the light faded... Time had become a stone. Silent. Empty. Yet still filled with immeasurable power. For many years thereafter, the Mage devoted himself to cruelty. Cities burned beneath his hand. Thousands perished. Kingdoms crumbled before him. And in time... He became known throughout the world as The Mad Wizard with the Yellow Stone.",
    "Many years passed. Then an Ancient Evil came forth and formed an alliance with the Mad Wizard. Together they gathered countless mages and prepared an invasion into the Worlds Beyond. Yet the Ancient Evil never intended for them to succeed. The Wizard and his army were sent ahead as little more than sacrifices—to test whether any beings dwelt within those distant realms.",
    "As they crossed the boundary between worlds, they were met by the guardians who had long watched over those sacred lands. The invaders were hopelessly outmatched. Though they fought with all the might they possessed, they could not withstand the strength of the realm's defenders. Many fell in battle, while others were captured and compelled to reveal the location of the Ancient Evil who had sent them.",
    "Thus the guardians journeyed to Moratal. There they struck down the Ancient Evil, bringing its reign to an end. In victory they claimed the relic they had long sought, ensuring that it would never again fall into the hands of those driven by greed.",
    "Thereafter, the guardians appointed faithful workers to watch over the relic without ceasing. Their charge was simple: That no mortal soul should ever possess it again.",
    "To this very day, those workers labour in secret. Their leader alone chooses the next soul within Moratal worthy of the task. That chosen one must venture into the unknown, recover the sacred stone, and secure it within the Cave of Time, that the workers of the Worlds Beyond might at last complete their long vigil and return to their home.",
    "Until that day comes... Moratal remains a land clouded by mystery. Kingdoms continue to hunger for power. Fear remains the weapon of rulers. The past is forgotten.",
    "Yet prophecy speaks of one who shall one day rise. One who shall be chosen by the Prasinos Wizard. One who shall venture into the unknown... To seek that which has long been lost.",
    "The Amber Stone.",
]

end_of_intro = "23 years later..."

